{
 "schemaVersion": 1,
 "id": "kukhnya-s01e02-scene-05",
 "pair": "ru-en",
 "title": "Японский нож  (The Japanese Knife)",
 "level": "A1 — Duolingo Section 2",
 "labels": {
  "nastya": "Настя",
  "senya": "Сеня"
 },
 "segments": [
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "While everyone searches, Nastya asks Senya why the chef can't just buy another knife. Senya explains what makes this one so special. Here is their talk in Russian first.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Почему нельзя купить такой нож?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "По-быстрому такой нож купить не получится.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "А сколько он стоит?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Это дорогой японский нож.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Шеф заказывал его очень долго.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "И он очень острый?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Самый острый нож на кухне.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Где же он может быть?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Мы уже везде искали.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Может, кто-то взял его домой?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Никто не посмеет это сделать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Шеф сразу всех уволит.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Давай нож ищи скорее.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Хорошо. Я посмотрю здесь.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's see why this knife is special.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Почему нельзя купить такой нож?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Why can't we buy such a knife?' The word for \"it's not allowed\" or \"it's impossible\" is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "нельзя",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ". Put ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Почему",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " in front and you can ask why anything can't be done.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "По-быстрому такой нож купить не получится.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You can't buy such a knife in a hurry.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "По-быстрому",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to \"in a quick way\", built from the word for \"quickly\". Then ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "не получится.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", literally \"it won't work out\", which Russians say whenever something can't be done.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "А сколько он стоит?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And how much does it cost?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "сколько он стоит?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to \"how much costs\", the shop question. Nastya calls the knife ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "он",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the term for \"he\", because the Russian language treats some objects like people.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Это дорогой японский нож.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'This is an expensive Japanese knife.' The word for expensive, ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "дорогой",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", does two jobs: it also translates to \"dear\", as in a dear friend. And there is no \"is\", just ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Это",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", literally \"this\", and the rest.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Шеф заказывал его очень долго.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The chef ordered it for a very long time.' The action word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "заказывал",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", literally \"ordered\", is built from the term for an order. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "его",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning \"it\", is the same word as \"him\" and \"his\", and it never changes.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "И он очень острый?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'And is it very sharp?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "острый?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to \"sharp\" and also \"spicy\", so the describing word is good for knives and for food. Context tells you which.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Самый острый нож на кухне.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The sharpest knife in the kitchen.' Put ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Самый",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " in front of a describing word and it translates to \"the most\": ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Самый острый",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to \"the most sharp\". It works with any describing word.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Где же он может быть?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Where could it possibly be?' The word for maybe is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "может быть?",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", but here the two words literally translate to \"can be\". Adding the little word ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "же",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " after ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Где",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " adds the \"possibly\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Мы уже везде искали.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We already looked everywhere.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "уже",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the term for already, and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "везде",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the term for everywhere, are small words you will use constantly. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "искали.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", literally \"looked for\", is built from ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "искали.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the same action word as the command below.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Может, кто-то взял его домой?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Maybe someone took it home?' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "может",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " on its own translates to \"maybe\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "кто-то",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to \"someone\", built from the word for \"who\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Никто не посмеет это сделать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Nobody would dare do that.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Никто не",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " literally translates to \"nobody not\", which is how Russians say nobody. ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "посмеет",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", meaning \"will dare\", is built from ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "посмеет",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", the term for to dare.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Шеф сразу всех уволит.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'The chef will fire everyone immediately.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "сразу",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the term for the everyday \"immediately\". The word for \"everyone\", ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "всех",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", takes a special ending because they are the ones receiving the action.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Давай нож ищи скорее.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Come on, look for the knife quickly.' ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Давай",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to a friendly \"come on\". ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "ищи",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " is the term for the command \"look for\", and ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "скорее.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": " translates to \"quicker\".",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Хорошо. Я посмотрю здесь.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'All right. I will look here.' The first part of ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "посмотрю",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ", literally \"I will look\", gives it the sense of a quick look. The word for \"here\" is ",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "здесь.",
   "gap": 0.25
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": ". Now let's listen to the whole conversation again from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Почему нельзя купить такой нож?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "По-быстрому такой нож купить не получится.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "А сколько он стоит?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Это дорогой японский нож.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Шеф заказывал его очень долго.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "И он очень острый?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Самый острый нож на кухне.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "nastya",
   "t": "Где же он может быть?",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
   "v": "senya",
   "t": "Мы уже везде искали.",
   "gap": 0.5
  },
  {
